# esp32s3-n32r16-00 -- ESP32-S3 N32R16 (32 MB flash, 16 MB PSRAM), MAC 38:44:be:cd:5e:94.
#
# A REAL FILE, NOT A SYMLINK, AND THERE IS ONLY ONE UNIT.  This was copied from
# esp32s3-n8r2-00.manifest, whose header describes a SYMLINKED PAIR of physical boards; that text
# was carried across verbatim by the copy and every clause of it was false here.  It is rewritten
# rather than trimmed because a manifest header is read by whoever is about to change the ship
# list, and a header describing a different board's arrangement is worse than none.
#
# WHY NOT A SYMLINK TO THE N8R2 LIST: this board is repartitioned for the llloader
# (w3_pio/partitions/partitions_32M_ota.csv -- factory/ota_0/storage) and has 26.8 MB of LittleFS
# against the N8R2's 1.5 MB.  The ship list is identical TODAY, but the reason to diverge already
# exists, and a symlink would make the first divergence silently edit the other board too.
#
# PIN MAP: boards/pins/esp32-s3-devkitc-1.scm, the generic S3 devkit pinout.  The source manifest
# named esp32s3-n8r2.scm; the two files are BYTE-IDENTICAL apart from a comment line, so nothing
# functional turns on this today -- but this board is not a YD-ESP32-23 and there is no evidence it
# shares that layout, so it should not claim to.  If a real N32R16 pinout is ever established, add
# boards/pins/esp32s3-n32r16.scm and point this line at it.
#
# An env with no manifest stages no data_staged/<env>/, and uploadfs then dies with
#   Building FS image from 'data' directory ... warning: can't read source directory
# which reads as a filesystem problem, not a missing manifest.

# Core runtime
core/setup.scm
core/Compiler.scm
core/Lobs.scm
core/Behaviors.scm
core/Terminal.scm
file: boards/pins/esp32-s3-devkitc-1.scm -> Pins.scm
core/Timers.scm
core/ESP32.scm
core/CommonIO.scm
core/Buzzer.scm
core/Sonar.scm
core/WiFi.scm
core/I2C.scm
core/Wire.scm
core/PCA9685.scm
core/PCF8574.scm
core/WS2812.scm
core/LightSensor.scm
core/LCD1602.scm
core/array.scm

# R5RS/R7RS overrides
rxrs/rxrs.scm
rxrs/rxrs_cxr.scm
rxrs/rxrs_exceptions.scm
rxrs/rxrs_continuations.scm
rxrs/rxrs_promises.scm
rxrs/rxrs_quasiquote.scm
rxrs/rxrs_syntax.scm
rxrs/rxrs_library.scm
rxrs/rxrs_srfi.scm

# Optional features
features/Neopixel.scm
features/rsa.scm
features/dh_groups.scm
features/csv.scm

# Dev tools
tools/llip-server.scm
# LLIP serial receiver -- setup.scm loads it when present (see core/setup.scm).
# NOTE ON WHAT A MANIFEST DECIDES: every target already RECEIVES all of the Scheme library --
# w3_make_release_one copies the whole scm/ tree into every package (w3_make.sh ~line 354).
# A manifest only chooses the DEFAULT on-device FS subset; anything omitted is still shipped
# and can be staged or loaded at runtime.  This file is listed because it must be RESIDENT AT
# BOOT to be useful: without it in the FS the board cannot accept `llip --serial PORT send`,
# so pushing one settings file costs a full filesystem upload through pio -- which also wipes
# .pio/build for every other env and forces concurrent sessions to rebuild.
features/llip-serial.scm

tools/test-framework.scm

# Board-specific init
boards/esp32s3-n8r2.scm

# Runtime defaults
runtime-defaults/Settings.scm
# Peer CA for the `network` test_id: written by _w3_run_network, absent otherwise (untracked).
optional: runtime-defaults/net-test-ca.pem -> net-test-ca.pem
# Bench WiFi credentials: untracked, absent by default, silent when absent (see .example).
optional: runtime-defaults/Settings-local.scm -> Settings-local.scm
runtime-defaults/Settings-Lamb.scm

# Test suite
# Perf/gcpause bench files only (small).  The correctness tiers (smoke/conform/subsystem/extend)
# are delivered INCREMENTALLY per-tier by _w3_run_correct_esp32 -- the full ~460KB ll_tests suite
# is NOT shipped to embedded FS.
file: tests/ll_tests/bench-runner.scm   -> ll_tests/bench-runner.scm
file: tests/ll_tests/benchmarks.scm     -> ll_tests/benchmarks.scm
file: tests/ll_tests/gc-pause-bench.scm -> ll_tests/gc-pause-bench.scm
file: tests/ll_tests/pause_bench.scm    -> ll_tests/pause_bench.scm
file: tests/ll_tests/ncg-fusion-probe.scm -> ll_tests/ncg-fusion-probe.scm
